The highest level function is collocate_and_store_date_range.
Example usage:

>> collocate_and_store_date_range([2009 1 1], [2009 12 31], 'cloudsat', 'cpr', 'noaa18', 'mhs')

This will collect collocations for a full year and write them to the disk. The
location it's written to depends on configuration settings in colloc_config.

TODO: more documentation

The highest level function that returns results (rather than writing them
away) is collocate_date.
Example usage of collocate_date:

>> [O D M] = collocate_date(2010, 2, 1, 'cloudsat', 'cpr', 'noaa18', 'mhs')
(...)
O = 

    noaa18: [173253x29 double]


D = 

    noaa18: [173253x45 double]


M = 

    noaa18: [3890x8 double]

Columns are documented at http://satpage/docs/datasets/collocations/ and
defined in colloc_config('cols_cpr_mhs') with the fields overlap, data and
meandata.
